Symbol datatype-
Uniqueness: Every Symbol is guaranteed to be unique, even if two symbols have the same description.
Primitive type: Like string, number, boolean, null, undefined, and bigint, symbol is a primitive.
Not auto-converted: Symbols don’t automatically convert to strings or numbers — trying to print them directly can throw errors unless you explicitly convert.
Use case: Often used as object property keys to avoid accidental overwriting.
eg;
let id1 = Symbol("id");
let id2 = Symbol("id");

console.log(id1 === id2); // false (unique even with same description)

let obj = {
    [id1]: "Muskan",
    [id2]: "Coder"
};

console.log(obj[id1]); // Muskan
console.log(obj[id2]); // Coder

