Strict equality and loose equality operator-
Strict equality (===),this means both the data-type and value are checked to determine equality , and it returns a booleans answer.
loose equality  (==),this means only the value is checked to determine equality, and it returns a boolean answer.
**== → Loose equality (compares values, allows type conversion).
!= → Loose inequality (opposite of ==, also allows type conversion).
=== → Strict equality (compares values and types, no conversion).
!== → Strict inequality (opposite of ===, true if value or type differ).

